---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LinkedText from '../components/LinkedText.astro';

// Constants from reference/XML/Infos/globalsInt.xml and culture.xml; mechanic
// transcribed from City.cs (getCaptureThreshold / setCaptureTurns / doTribeTurn).
//
//   CITY_BASE_CAPTURE_TURNS      = 2
//   CITY_CAPTURE_DAMAGE_PERCENT  = 50   (HP the city is left at after it flips)
//   culture.iExtraCaptureTurns:  Weak 0 · Developing 1 · Strong 2 · Legendary 3
//   +1 to the threshold when the capturer is NOT the city's original founder.

const BASE_TURNS = 2;

const cultures = [
  { name: 'Weak',       extra: 0 },
  { name: 'Developing', extra: 1 },
  { name: 'Strong',     extra: 2 },
  { name: 'Legendary',  extra: 3 },
];

// threshold = max(1, base + cultureExtra + (notFounder ? 1 : 0))
const rows = cultures.map(c => ({
  culture: c.name,
  extra: c.extra,
  foreign: Math.max(1, BASE_TURNS + c.extra + 1), // taking a city you didn't found
  own:     Math.max(1, BASE_TURNS + c.extra),     // retaking a city your team founded
}));
---

<Base
  title="City Capture Mechanics"
  active="city-capture-mechanics"
  pageMark="🏰"
  description="How long a city takes to change hands after you occupy it in Old World. Covers the capture turns counter, the threshold formula of base plus enemy culture level plus the bonus for being the original founder, and the rules for gaining and losing progress each turn, transcribed from City.cs."
  pageStats={[
    { label: 'base turns', value: BASE_TURNS },
    { label: 'capture HP left', value: '50%' },
  ]}
>
  <p class="lede">
    Taking a city is not instant. When your unit occupies an enemy city, a
    hidden <b>capture turns counter</b> rises each turn you hold it, and the city
    changes hands only when the counter reaches its <b>threshold</b>. If you leave
    or are pushed off before then, the progress unwinds. The threshold depends on
    the city's <b>culture level</b> and on whether you founded it yourself.
  </p>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">How the counter works</h2>
    <ul class="cc-bullets">
      <li>
        Each turn your unit is actively occupying the city
        (<code>isUnitCapturingCity</code>), the counter increases by
        <b>+1</b> (<code>changeCaptureTurns(1)</code>).
      </li>
      <li>
        The city changes hands the moment the counter reaches
        <code>getCaptureThreshold()</code>, and the city is left
        <b>damaged to 50% HP</b> (<code>CITY_CAPTURE_DAMAGE_PERCENT</code>).
      </li>
      <li>
        While no one is occupying it, the counter falls by <b>1</b> per turn back
        to 0, so an interrupted capture is undone. You must hold the city
        <b>continuously</b> for the full count.
      </li>
      <li>
        A recapture or a liberation also resets the counter to 0 when ownership
        changes (<code>setCaptureTurns(0)</code>).
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">The threshold formula</h2>
    <div class="cc-formula">
      <div class="cc-line">
        <span class="cc-eq">turns = CITY_BASE_CAPTURE_TURNS&nbsp;(2)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-line">
        <span class="cc-eq cc-add">+ culture(highest&nbsp;enemy&nbsp;culture).iExtraCaptureTurns</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-line">
        <span class="cc-eq cc-add">+ 1&nbsp;&nbsp;if you are not the city's original founder</span>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-line cc-min">
        <span class="cc-eq">→ minimum 1</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      The culture term uses the <b>highest culture level of any team other than
      the capturer</b> that has culture in the city, which is how deeply the
      defender is established there. The values come from
      <code>iExtraCaptureTurns</code> in <code>culture.xml</code>.
    </p>

    <table class="cc-table cc-table--narrow">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>City culture</th><th class="cc-num">Extra turns</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {cultures.map(c => (
          <tr>
            <td><LinkedText text={c.name} /></td>
            <td class="cc-num"><b>+{c.extra}</b></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="cc-fineprint">
      The <b>+1 for not being the founder</b> term is <code>getCaptureTeam() !=
      getFirstTeam()</code>, and it applies when you take a city your team did
      <b>not</b> found. <b>Retaking a city you once held is one turn faster</b>,
      and the test is the team that originally founded the city, even when an
      enemy captured and grew it since.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">Turns to flip</h2>
    <p>
      The table gives the hold time you need, by the city's culture level and by
      whether you founded it.
    </p>
    <table class="cc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>City culture</th>
          <th class="cc-num">Taking a foreign city</th>
          <th class="cc-num">Retaking your own</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map(r => (
          <tr>
            <td><LinkedText text={r.culture} /> <span class="cc-dim">(+{r.extra})</span></td>
            <td class="cc-num"><b>{r.foreign}</b></td>
            <td class="cc-num"><b>{r.own}</b></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="cc-fineprint">
      A newly founded enemy outpost therefore changes hands after <b>3</b> turns
      of unbroken occupation, and an old <LinkedText text="Legendary" /> enemy
      capital takes <b>6</b>. Liberating one of your own cities takes a turn off
      each of those.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">When a captured city is razed instead</h2>
    <p>
      The city normally transfers when the counter reaches the threshold. It is
      <b>razed</b> instead in the two cases below (<code>setCaptureTurns</code>).
    </p>
    <ul class="cc-bullets">
      <li>
        A <LinkedText text="Tribe" /> captures it and the
        <code>GAMEOPTION_ALLOW_CITY_RAZING</code> option is on.
      </li>
      <li>
        A player captures it while already at their <b>city cap</b>
        (<code>isCityMaxReached()</code>), so they cannot hold another and the city
        burns.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="cc-section">
    <h2 class="cc-h2">Worked example</h2>
    <ol class="cc-steps">
      <li>
        You assault a rival's <LinkedText text="Strong" />-culture city (you did
        not found it). Threshold = 2 (base) + 2 (Strong) + 1 (not founder) =
        <b>5</b>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your unit occupies the city, and the counter rises through 1, 2, 3, 4 and
        5 at the end of each turn it holds.
      </li>
      <li>
        If a relief force evicts your unit on turn 3, with the counter at 3, the
        counter falls by 1 per turn back toward 0 and you have to start over.
      </li>
      <li>
        Hold all 5 turns and the city passes to you at <b>50% HP</b>. Had the same
        city originally been <i>yours</i>, it would have passed to you in
        <b>4</b>.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <p class="cc-source">
    Source: <code>City.cs</code>, namely <code>getCaptureThreshold()</code> for
    the formula, <code>setCaptureTurns()</code> for the transfer, the razing and
    the 50% damage, and the counter changes in <code>doTribeTurn()</code>.
    Constants come from <code>globalsInt.xml</code>
    (<code>CITY_BASE_CAPTURE_TURNS</code>, <code>CITY_CAPTURE_DAMAGE_PERCENT</code>)
    and <code>culture.xml</code> (<code>iExtraCaptureTurns</code>).
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .lede b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-section { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .cc-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .cc-section p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin: 0.3rem 0;
  }
  .cc-section p b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-bullets {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    max-width: 80ch;
  }
  .cc-bullets li { padding: 0.2rem 0; }
  .cc-bullets b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-formula {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0.9rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .cc-line { padding: 0.12rem 0; }
  .cc-eq {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .cc-add { color: var(--text-dim); }
  .cc-min .cc-eq { color: var(--accent); }

  .cc-table {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 64ch;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 0.6rem 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .cc-table--narrow { max-width: 36ch; }
  .cc-table thead th {
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }
  .cc-table tbody td {
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .cc-table tbody tr:hover { background: var(--bg-elev); }
  .cc-num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .cc-num b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .cc-dim { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: 0.8em; }

  .cc-steps {
    list-style: decimal inside;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 72ch;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .cc-steps li { padding: 0.25rem 0; }
  .cc-steps b { color: var(--text); }

  .cc-fineprint {
    color: var(--text-faint) !important;
    font-size: 0.78rem !important;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-style: italic;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .cc-fineprint b { color: var(--text-dim); }

  .cc-source {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 80ch;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78em;
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    padding: 0 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
